 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Colours",
     "texto": [
      "Almost all the basic colours are -i adjectives: **あかい** (red), **あおい** (blue), **しろい** (white), **くろい** (black), **きいろい** (yellow).",
      "They go before the noun: **くろい ジャケット** (black jacket).",
      "**の** can replace a noun already mentioned, like «the one» in English: **あおい の** (the blue one), **やすい の** (the cheap one)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "In the shop",
     "texto": [
      "**これ を ください** = I'll take this one.",
      "**もっと** = more. **もっと やすい の は あります か** (do you have a cheaper one?).",
      "**そして** links two sentences: «and also»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Comparing with より",
     "texto": [
      "**より** means «than» in comparisons and goes after what is being compared: **A は B より やすい です** (A is cheaper than B).",
      "The adjective **does not change**: unlike English, there is no special form for «cheaper»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
